,{\"id\":\"collapsed_dish_frame\",\"verdict\":\"match\",\"evidence\":\"reading: \\\"A dish on a stand (clear)\\\" — \\\"a thin arm reaching from the rim to a knob suspended over the centre; the dish rim is dented and split on the lower right\\\"\",\"why\":\"A dish with a feed arm on a base is the named object, and the dented, split rim supports the collapsed claim.\",\"suggested_id\":\"\",\"flag_for_human\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"shredded_antenna_mesh\",\"verdict\":\"loose\",\"evidence\":\"reading: \\\"A rod with crossbars (partial)\\\" — \\\"One long diagonal shaft carrying about ten short bars set across it at intervals, several of them kinked or snapped off short\\\"\",\"why\":\"A shaft with crossbars is an antenna and the snapped elements support damage, but nothing in the reading is a mesh, so the flavour text must not describe woven or shredded mesh.\",\"suggested_id\":\"\",\"flag_for_human\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"cracked_battery_pallet\",\"verdict\":\"loose\",\"evidence\":\"reading: \\\"A boxy unit in a yellow frame (partial)\\\" — \\\"A dark grey slab body wrapped in a thick yellow border, tilted on its side\\\"; condition: intact\",\"why\":\"A boxed unit in a protective frame is consistent with a battery pallet, but the reader recorded it as intact, so the crack in the name has no support in the drawing.\",\"suggested_id\":\"\",\"flag_for_human\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"seized_reaction_wheel_housing\",\"verdict\":\"match\",\"evidence\":\"reading: \\\"A spoked wheel (clear)\\\" — \\\"Eight spokes running from a small central hub to a wide flat rim, shown flat-on; a short notch breaks the rim at the lower right\\\"\",\"why\":\"A reaction wheel housing is a spoked wheel around a hub, and nothing in the reading contradicts the name.\",\"suggested_id\":\"\",\"flag_for_human\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"burst_pressurant_sphere\",\"verdict\":\"mismatch\",\"evidence\":\"reading: \\\"A cluster of broken rock (partial)\\\" — \\\"Three or four angular chunks with dark pitted faces and pale chipped edges pressed together... no flat or manufactured surfaces\\\"\",\"why\":\"The reader explicitly found no manufactured surfaces and nothing spherical or vessel-like, so this is natural debris rather than a pressure vessel; no id is suggested because the reading is only partial.\",\"suggested_id\":\"\",\"flag_for_human\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"delaminated_radiator_fin\",\"verdict\":\"loose\",\"evidence\":\"reading: \\\"A flat metal bracket plate (clear)\\\" — \\\"An irregular stepped grey plate with six small bolt holes near its corners and two short scratch lines\\\"; condition: intact\",\"why\":\"A flat grey plate is the right family for a radiator fin, but the reading shows a bolted bracket with only surface scratches, so there is no delamination and no radiator detail to write about.\",\"suggested_id\":\"\",\"flag_for_human\":\"Sprite shows a solid bolted metal plate described as intact, yet the piece carries the FRAGILE flag — art and tuning disagree.\"},{\"id\":\"torn_solar_wing_spar\",\"verdict\":\"loose\",\"evidence\":\"reading: \\\"Two solar panels (clear)\\\" — \\\"A pair of tall rectangular wings side by side, each ruled into a grid of dark blue cells... the right wing is tilted slightly out of line\\\"; condition: intact\",\"why\":\"The drawing is plainly a solar wing, but it shows the cell panels rather than a spar and the reader called it intact, so neither the spar nor the tear is supported beyond the slight misalignment.\",\"suggested_id\":\"\",\"flag_for_human\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"cracked_optics_barrel\",\"verdict\":\"loose\",\"evidence\":\"reading: \\\"A camera lens (clear)\\\" — \\\"A short cylinder lying on its side with a ringed barrel and a round dark front element holding a bright cyan glint\\\"; condition: intact\",\"why\":\"A ringed barrel with a front lens element is an optics barrel, but the reader recorded it as intact with a clean glinting element, so the crack in the name is not drawn.\",\"suggested_id\":\"\",\"flag_for_human\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"frac