e with bevelled corners holding pale blue glass, cracks radiating from a dark star-shaped hole in the centre\\\"\",\"why\":\"A bevelled housing holding a cracked glass aperture is the optical face of a star tracker, and the radiating cracks support the shattered claim.\",\"suggested_id\":\"\",\"flag_for_human\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"warped_gyro_deck\",\"verdict\":\"loose\",\"evidence\":\"reading: \\\"A control box with wires (clear)\\\" — \\\"An upright grey cabinet with a blue screen, a grid of small holes, two rows of coloured indicator strips and buttons\\\"; condition: intact\",\"why\":\"An instrumented electronics cabinet is a fair reading of an avionics deck, but the reader found it intact and square, so nothing in the drawing is warped.\",\"suggested_id\":\"\",\"flag_for_human\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"cracked_ablative_nose_cone\",\"verdict\":\"match\",\"evidence\":\"reading: \\\"A pointed shield-shaped shell (partial)\\\" — \\\"A tapering grey cone or nose piece with a narrow raised rib down the middle and a jagged broken edge along the bottom\\\"\",\"why\":\"A tapering nose shell with a jagged broken edge matches both the object and the cracked condition in the name.\",\"suggested_id\":\"\",\"flag_for_human\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"split_avionics_rack\",\"verdict\":\"loose\",\"evidence\":\"reading: \\\"A circuit board (clear)\\\" — \\\"A green rectangular board with two large black chips... and a row of gold contact fingers along the bottom edge\\\"; condition: intact\",\"why\":\"A populated circuit board is avionics, but the reading shows one whole undamaged card rather than a split rack chassis, so the flavour text must not lean on the rack or the split.\",\"suggested_id\":\"\",\"flag_for_human\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"torn_reactor_shield_plate\",\"verdict\":\"mismatch\",\"evidence\":\"reading: \\\"A broken circuit board piece (partial)\\\" — \\\"A jagged green fragment with two yellow stripes and a couple of small chips, a separated splinter floating to its left and a curled rust-brown wire hanging below\\\"\",\"why\":\"A green board fragment with components and a wire is electronics, not a slab of reactor shielding; no id is suggested because the reading is only partial.\",\"suggested_id\":\"\",\"flag_for_human\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"cracked_deep_space_dish\",\"verdict\":\"match\",\"evidence\":\"reading: \\\"A parabolic dish on a mount (clear)\\\" — \\\"A grey dish seen at a three-quarter angle with a strut-mounted feed arm crossing its face... the rim is dented and irregular\\\"\",\"why\":\"A parabolic dish with a feed arm is the named antenna, and the dented irregular rim supports the damage claim.\",\"suggested_id\":\"\",\"flag_for_human\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"fused_ion_grid_assembly\",\"verdict\":\"loose\",\"evidence\":\"reading: \\\"An empty picture frame with broken glass (partial)\\\" — \\\"A square dark-blue frame whose interior holds only pale cyan shards angled inward from the corners, leaving a hollow middle\\\"\",\"why\":\"A square frame carrying an inner element fits a grid assembly, but the interior is empty apart from shards, so nothing shows a grid and shattered is the opposite of fused.\",\"suggested_id\":\"\",\"flag_for_human\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"severed_boom_mast\",\"verdict\":\"mismatch\",\"evidence\":\"reading: \\\"A length of tangled cable (partial)\\\" — \\\"A twisted braided rope-like strand running diagonally, frayed and splayed into a bristly knot at the upper right end\\\"\",\"why\":\"A braided flexible strand is a cable or tether, not a rigid boom mast, so only the severed end survives the comparison; no id is suggested because the reading is only partial.\",\"suggested_id\":\"\",\"flag_for_human\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"scorched_fuel_cell_stack\",\"verdict\":\"loose\",\"evidence\":\"reading: \\\"A tray of batteries (clear)\\\" — \\\"A grey open-topped case divided into compartments holding blocky cells, each with coloured bars — yellow, red, orange — marking charge levels\\\"; condition: intact\",\"why\":\"A case of stacked power cells is the right object, but the reader found it intact with bright charge indicators and no soot, so nothing in the drawing is scorched.\",\"suggested_id\":\"\",\"flag_for_human\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"shattered_cryo_dewar\",\"verdict\":\"mismatch\",\"evidence\":\"reading: \\\"A water tank (clear)\\\" — \\\"`H2O` is stencilled in dark letters across the middle panel\\\"; condition: intact\",\"why\":\"The stencilled H2O the artist drew makes this a water tank rather than a cryogenic dewar, and the reader found it intact rather than shattered.\",\"suggested_id\":\"potable_water_tank\",\"flag_for_human\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"impact_pitted_engine_bell\",\"verdict\":\"match\",\"evidence\":\"reading: \\\"A bell-shaped nozzle (clear)\\\" — \\\"A flared cone standing upright with stacked ring ridges down its body, a dark sooty throat, and a rust-brown crusted rim at the base\\\"\",\"why\":\"A flared, ring-stiffened nozzle with a sooty throat and crusted rim is an engine bell showing surface damage, as the name claims.\",\"suggested_id\":\"\",\"flag_for_human\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"cracked_command_module_hatch\",\"verdict\":\"mismatch\",\"evidence\":\"reading: \\\"A hex nut (clear)\\\" — \\\"A small six-sided ring seen face-on with a round hole through the middle and a light highlight on the upper left; nothing else in the cell\\\"\",\"why\":\"A plain six-sided fastener is a different object from a crew hatch, and the reader found nothing cracked or hatch-like in the cell.\",\"suggested_id\":\"hex_nut_fastener\",\"flag_for_human\":\"A solid steel nut drawn intact carries the FRAGILE flag — art and tuning disagree.\"},{\"id\":\"armstrongs_module\",\"verdict\":\"match\",\"evidence\":\"reading: \\\"A metal canister (clear)\\\" — \\\"A grey cylinder lying diagonally with rimmed ends and two yellow bands around its body; the lower left end is dented and a small chip is broken off beside it\\\"\",\"why\":\"A banded cylinder with rimmed ends is a service module body, and the dent and broken chip 